<title>TUNISIA: Tunisian news agency TAP has a new chief.</title>
<headline>Tunisian news agency TAP has a new chief.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tunisian Information Ministry on Wednesday announced that Brahim Fridhi was named as new chairman of the state-run Tunisian news agency Tunis Afrique Presse (TAP).</p>
<p>Fridhi, who was director of the French language daily newspaper Le Renouveau owned by the ruling party the Constitutional Democratic Rally (RCD), replaces Mohamed Mahfoudh.</p>
